{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "VR-Reader",
    "steam_appid": 3668710,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Read manga, comics, magazines and photos from your harddrive in VR.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Zoomable and grabbable pages</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Intuitive controls designed for manga/comics and small text</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Close reading mode</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Quick focus</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Page tilting</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Great resolution &amp; image compression </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supported files in early access: <strong>pdf</strong>, <strong>cbz</strong>, <strong>zip</strong>, <strong>jpg</strong>, <strong>jpeg</strong>,\u00a0<strong>png</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No advertising or other hidden costs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No online store, you have to have the content in your PC</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Low system requirements. Tested on an older laptop with an AMD Ryzen 5 3550H, 8GB RAM, and an Nvidia GTX 1050, using a Meta Quest 2 via Steam Link.  </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3668710/extras/bbcd610e5adecc52e1457a3b8fd073b5.poster.avif?t=1749042806\" width=540 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3668710/extras/bbcd610e5adecc52e1457a3b8fd073b5.webm?t=1749042806\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3668710/extras/bbcd610e5adecc52e1457a3b8fd073b5.mp4?t=1749042806\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Handling the pages and reading in VR works a little differently than in real life. Here are two ways I've found it to be better and more enjoyable in VR than in real life.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >FULL PAGE MODE</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Focus the page</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Zoom so you see the whole page at once</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn tilting toggle on from book settings</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Press left/right to turn the whole page normally and use Focus when necessary</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >CLOSE READING MODE</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn tilting off from book settings</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use focus to center the page</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pressing up/down keeps the page in close, and pulls it from up to down</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Day 1 update v0.8.3: </strong>Analog stick deadzone slider, and early keyboard support. More info in Community Hub (button on upper side of the Steam page).</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Read manga, comics, magazines and photos from your harddrive in VR.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Zoomable and grabbable pages</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Intuitive controls designed for manga/comics and small text</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Close reading mode</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Quick focus</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Page tilting</p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Great resolution &amp; image compression </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supported files in early access: <strong>pdf</strong>, <strong>cbz</strong>, <strong>zip</strong>, <strong>jpg</strong>, <strong>jpeg</strong>,\u00a0<strong>png</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No advertising or other hidden costs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No online store, you have to have the content in your PC</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Low system requirements. Tested on an older laptop with an AMD Ryzen 5 3550H, 8GB RAM, and an Nvidia GTX 1050, using a Meta Quest 2 via Steam Link.  </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3668710/extras/bbcd610e5adecc52e1457a3b8fd073b5.poster.avif?t=1749042806\" width=540 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3668710/extras/bbcd610e5adecc52e1457a3b8fd073b5.webm?t=1749042806\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3668710/extras/bbcd610e5adecc52e1457a3b8fd073b5.mp4?t=1749042806\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Handling the pages and reading in VR works a little differently than in real life. Here are two ways I've found it to be better and more enjoyable in VR than in real life.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >FULL PAGE MODE</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Focus the page</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Zoom so you see the whole page at once</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn tilting toggle on from book settings</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Press left/right to turn the whole page normally and use Focus when necessary</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >CLOSE READING MODE</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn tilting off from book settings</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use focus to center the page</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pressing up/down keeps the page in close, and pulls it from up to down</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Day 1 update v0.8.3: </strong>Analog stick deadzone slider, and early keyboard support. More info in Community Hub (button on upper side of the Steam page).</p>",
    "short_description": "Read manga, magazines and photos in VR. Intuitive controls and zoomable pages are designed for reading small text.",
